From 29a22d25c2e4c27732cb5558864fa69f98818586 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:21:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] Pads: flicker-free dimming at low brightness

The PIC dims the LEDs by time: each step of its LED scan is lit for the
refresh time and dark for the dimmer interval. 1.2.1 keeps their sum at 23
down to 40 % (refresh 8); below that the refresh time stays at 8 and the
dark time grows 1.2x per step, so the whole scan slows down: at 4 % (the
menu's lowest) 8 + 112 = 120, 5.2 times the period at full brightness, at
0 % (SHIFT + LEARN + vertical encoder) 8 + 148 = 156, 6.8 times. That is
the flicker. Refresh times of 9 and below also give wrong colours on some
pads (upstream discussion #1869).

Flicker-free dimming (community feature, on by default): the PIC dims only
as far as its scan keeps the period of 23 with a refresh time of 10 or more
(43.5 % light; from 48 % up the timing is 1.2.1's), and the rest is done by
scaling the values sent to the PIC, in PIC::send() for every pad and sidebar
colour (all views, blinks, scrolls, greyout) and for the gold knob
indicators: scale = 1.2.1's light / the PIC's, so each level gives the light
it gave (the PIC's PWM being linear in the value). Values are rounded, a lit
channel stays at least 1. A change of brightness or of the setting sends the
pads and knob indicators again. Button LEDs and the 7-segment display are on
or off, and the PIC's own flash colours (fast play cursor) aren't values:
those are only dimmed down to 43.5 %. Off sends exactly what 1.2.1 sends.
See hid/led/pad_dimming.h. The setting is in CommunityFeatures.XML
(flickerFreeDimming); no new flash bytes.

Also: with settings never saved in flash (firmware type unknown) the pad
brightness stayed 0, i.e. 0 %; resetSettings() now sets it to full.

